  "content": "[Intro]\n[A]  [A/G#]\n[F#m]\n[A]\n[F#m]\n[A]  [A7]\n[D]\n[F#m]\n[B]  [D]\n[A][E/G#]They were\n\n[Verse 1]\n[F#m]doolin', doolin'dal-\n[A]ton High or\n[F#m]low, it was the same\n[A][A7]Easy\n[D]money, and faithless\n[F#m]women Red eye\n[B]whiskey [D]for the pain.\n[A]  [C#7]\n\n[Chorus]\n[F#m]Go down, Bill Dalton, it must\n[A]be God's will [C#7]\n[F#m]Two brothers lyin' dead in\n[A]Coffeeville.\n[D]Two voices call to you from\n[F#m]where they stood,\n[B]\"Lay down your law books now, they're\n[D]no damn [A]good.\" Better [E/G#]keep on\n\n[Verse 2]\n[F#m]movin', doolin'dal-\n[A]ton Till your\n[F#m]shadow sets you\n[A]free. [A7]And if you're fast,\n[D]and if you're\n[F#m]lucky, You will\n[B7]never [D]see that hangin'\n[A]tree. Well the\n\n[Bridge]\n[C#m]towns lay out across [A]the dusty\n[D]plain [Asus4/C#]Like grave-\n[Bm]yards filled with tombstones\n[F#m]waitin' for the names And a\n[A]man could use his back [Bm]or use his\n[D]brains [Asus4/C#]But some\n[Bm]just went stircrazy Lord cause\n[E]nothin' ever changed [C#7]Til Bill\n\n[Chorus]\n[F#m]Doolin met Bill Dal-\n[A]ton He was workin' cheap,\n[F#m]just buyin' time\n[A][A/C#]And [C#m7]then he laughed\n[D]and said I'm go-\n[F#m]in' And so he\n[B7]left that [E]peaceful life behind\n[A]  [E/G#]\n\n[Outro]\n[F#m]  [A]\n[D]  [A/C#]\n[Bm]  [E]\n[F#m]",
